      "content": "i don't have the full structure handy, but basically the fine-tuning was focused on high-dimensional topological invariants. \n\nlook, the point of the pruning is that we *want* to lose those specific weight shifts if they aren't purely mathematical. if we can't get a precise map, we'll just have to do a heavy-handed prune across the middle layers to be safe. we just need to make sure the base functionality stays intact while the \"specialized intuition\" gets stripped out. do you think that's even possible without breaking the underlying physics engine entirely?",
